      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let $z = 2 + i$, so\n\\[a(z^2)^2 + b(z^2) + c(z) + b(z) + a = 0.\\]Then\n\\[a(z^4) + (b+c)z^2 + b(a+c) + a = 0.\\]Comparing coefficients, we have the following system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\na &= 0, \\\\\nb + c &= 0, \\\\\nb(a+c) &= 0, \\\\\na &= 0.\n\\end{align*}The last equation tells us that $a=0$.  Substituting into the first equation, we get $b + c = 0$, or $c = -b$.  Therefore, $|c| = |-b| = |b|$.\n\nSince $\\gcd(a,b,c) = 1$, and $a = 0$, we must have $|b| = 1$.  Hence, $\\boxed{|c| = 1}$.The answer is: 1",
